---
// Alternative landing page for Google Ads testing (noindex, not in nav/sitemap).
// Positioning test: "Stop paying for intelligence twice" / learning-exhaust angle.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="KYDE, Stop Paying for Intelligence Twice"
  description="The trust boundary and learning infrastructure for enterprise AI. One gateway intercepts your agentic learning exhaust, secures your institutional alpha, and enforces behavioral guardrails, with zero code changes."
  noindex={true}
>
  <Navbar />
  <main>

    <!-- ══════════ HERO ══════════ -->
    <section class="relative bg-[#050505] overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-grid opacity-[0.06] pointer-events-none"></div>
      <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 pt-32 pb-20 md:border-x md:border-[#1F1F1F]">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h1 class="hero-h1 text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-white uppercase tracking-tight leading-[1.05] mb-6">
            Stop paying for<br />intelligence twice.
          </h1>
          <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-white uppercase tracking-[0.12em] leading-snug mb-5">
            The Trust Boundary &amp; Learning Infrastructure for Enterprise AI.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-white/50 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-8">
            KYDE is the single gateway that intercepts your agentic learning exhaust, secures your institutional alpha, and enforces strict behavioral guardrails, with zero code changes.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-10 font-mono text-sm">
            <span class="text-[#3DDC84]">$</span> <span class="text-white/50">export OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://gateway.kyde.intranet/v1</span>
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
            <button
              onclick="openModal()"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-white/40 text-white px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:border-white hover:bg-white/10 transition-all"
            >
              Talk to Us →
            </button>
            <a
              href="/starter"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white text-[#0A0A0A] px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:bg-[#E5E5E5] transition-all"
            >
              Start Free →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 01 · REVERSE INFORMATION PARADOX ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#0C0C0C]">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24 md:border-x md:border-[#1F1F1F]">
        <div class="mb-12">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-[#1F1F1F] pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#A8A8A8]">01 · The Reverse Information Paradox</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] leading-tight mb-6">
              When you consume intelligence, you create it. Who owns the output?
            </h2>
            <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed mb-4">
              When you buy AI, you pay for it twice: once in subscription fees, and again with the proprietary knowledge your employees and agents reveal to make the AI useful.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed">
              Every prompt, every tool execution, and, most importantly, <strong class="text-[#F2F2F2]">every manual correction your team makes when an agent fails</strong> is "learning exhaust." Right now, this exhaust flows upstream to train your vendor's next model. You are paying to privatize your own competitive advantage into someone else's infrastructure.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#141414] p-6 md:p-8 mb-6">
              <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FEC106] mb-4">The Reverse Information Paradox</p>
              <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed">
                The better you want a model to perform, the more of your unique institutional knowledge you must feed it. Over time, the model provider learns everything about how your business runs, while you learn nothing about how their model makes decisions.
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed">
              KYDE establishes a <strong class="text-[#F2F2F2]">hard trust boundary</strong> at your network edge. We capture this learning exhaust, keep it in your own tenant, and use it to compound <em>your</em> organization's intelligence, not your vendors'.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 02 · ARCHITECTURE ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#050505]">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24 md:border-x md:border-[#1F1F1F]">
        <div class="mb-12">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-[#1F1F1F] pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#A8A8A8]">02 · Architecture</span></div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] leading-tight mb-6 max-w-2xl">
          One gateway. Every agent. Zero code changes.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
          KYDE does not run inside the agent or on the host machine. It sits in the critical path as an active gateway. Every action, API call, and output passes through KYDE, where it is inspected, scoped, and signed <em>before</em> it executes.
        </p>

        <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#0C0C0C] p-6 md:p-8 mb-10 overflow-x-auto">
          <pre class="font-mono text-xs md:text-sm text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed">{`              [ YOUR AGENT FLEET ]
 (Claude, GPT-5, LangChain, Custom Bots, MCP Tools)
                       │
                       ▼
                ================
                █  KYDE GATEWAY █ ◄── Policy, Identity & Audit
                ================
                       │
     ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐
     ▼                 ▼                 ▼
[ THE PAST ]     [ THE PRESENT ]   [ THE FUTURE ]
Audit Ledger     Active Firewall   Learning Loop
(Tamper-proof)   (DLP & Block)     (IP & FinOps)`}</pre>
        </div>

        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-6">The Gateway spec</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          {[
            { k: "Zero code changes",    v: "Just point your SDKs to the KYDE proxy." },
            { k: "Target <100ms latency", v: "A highly optimized interception pipeline in the critical path." },
            { k: "Provider-agnostic",    v: "Works with OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, and local open-source models." },
            { k: "MCP-ready",            v: "Native support for the Model Context Protocol." },
          ].map(({ k, v }) => (
            <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#0C0C0C] p-5">
              <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#F2F2F2] mb-2">{k}</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed">{v}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 03 · ONE DATA STREAM ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#0C0C0C]">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24 md:border-x md:border-[#1F1F1F]">
        <div class="mb-12">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-[#1F1F1F] pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#A8A8A8]">03 · One data stream. Three dimensions.</span></div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] leading-tight mb-6 max-w-2xl">
          Why build a wall when you can build a compound engine?
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
          Because KYDE sits in the critical path, every agent transaction leaves a cryptographically signed entry. We read this single data stream in three directions to serve your Security, Legal, and Financial teams.
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-16">
          {[
            { t: "Past",    n: "Audit Ledger",     q: "Prove what happened" },
            { t: "Present", n: "Active Firewall",  q: "Prevent the damage" },
            { t: "Future",  n: "Metric Scorecard", q: "Compound your learning" },
          ].map(({ t, n, q }) => (
            <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#050505] p-5 text-center">
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-2">{t}</p>
              <p class="font-mono text-sm text-[#F2F2F2] mb-1">{n}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#A8A8A8]">"{q}"</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <!-- 03.1 PROVE -->
        <div class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] pt-12 mb-16">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-4">03.1 · The Past: Prove</p>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] leading-tight mb-5">
                The suspect can't write the police report.
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed">
                Your LLM provider's log lives on their servers, signed with their keys. In a legal or compliance dispute, it holds no independent weight. KYDE's audit trail is architecturally independent, <strong class="text-[#F2F2F2]">Ed25519-signed</strong>, and <strong class="text-[#F2F2F2]">hash-chained</strong> before any token leaves your network.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              {[
                { label: "Immutable forensics",  desc: "Every action is cryptographically linked to the previous one (#a4d1 references #a4d0). If an agent attempts to alter its history, the chain breaks." },
                { label: "Undeletable by design", desc: "No agent, not even one with admin access, can modify or delete its own trajectory logs." },
                { label: "Instant compliance",   desc: "Automatically generate audit-ready reports for GDPR, DORA, and NIS-2 auditors." },
              ].map(({ label, desc }) => (
                <div class="flex items-start gap-4 border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#141414] p-4">
                  <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-[#3DDC84] mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
                  <div>
                    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F2F2F2] mb-0.5">{label}</p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-[#A8A8A8]">{desc}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 03.2 PREVENT -->
        <div class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] pt-12 mb-16">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-4">03.2 · The Present: Prevent</p>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] leading-tight mb-5">
                Deterministic guardrails on probabilistic tech.
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed mb-8">
                An audit log tells you <em>why</em> you crashed. A firewall prevents the crash. KYDE intercepts data in real time, executing deny-by-default policies at the boundary before the model provider ever sees the payload.
              </p>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                {[
                  { label: "Active DLP",         desc: "Automatically redact personally identifiable information (PII) and corporate intellectual property before it leaves your tenant." },
                  { label: "Behavioral scoping", desc: "Limit what tools an agent can call based on its cryptographic identity. If a customer-service bot attempts to query the payroll database, KYDE drops the connection." },
                  { label: "Loop interdiction",  desc: "Detect and kill recursive token-spend loops (agents talking to agents in infinite, expensive retries) before they drain your API budget." },
                ].map(({ label, desc }) => (
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-4 border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#141414] p-4">
                    <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-[#FF5C5C] mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M18.364 5.636l-12.728 12.728M5.636 5.636l12.728 12.728" /></svg>
                    <div>
                      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F2F2F2] mb-0.5">{label}</p>
                      <p class="text-xs text-[#A8A8A8]">{desc}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#050505]">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-white/8 px-4 py-3">
                <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF5C5C]/40"></span>
                <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#FFB84D]/40"></span>
                <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#3DDC84]/40"></span>
                <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-[10px] text-white/20">intercept</span>
              </div>
              <div class="p-5 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto">
                <p class="text-white/25 mb-2">// Incoming trace: agent:support-02 ──&gt; api.openai.com</p>
                <p class="text-white/40">&#123;</p>
                <p class="text-white/40 pl-4">"prompt": "Confirm contract value of €1.2M with j.mueller@acme.com..."</p>
                <p class="text-white/40 mb-4">&#125;</p>
                <p class="text-white/25 mb-2">// KYDE intercept: policy [dlp-standard] active (12ms)</p>
                <p class="text-white/40">&#123;</p>
                <p class="pl-4"><span class="text-white/40">"action": </span><span class="text-[#FF5C5C]">"MASK"</span><span class="text-white/40">,</span></p>
                <p class="text-white/40 pl-4">"reason": "PII &amp; financial data detected",</p>
                <p class="pl-4"><span class="text-white/40">"payload": "Confirm contract value of </span><span class="text-[#3DDC84]">[REDACTED_FIN]</span><span class="text-white/40"> with </span><span class="text-[#3DDC84]">[REDACTED_EMAIL]</span><span class="text-white/40">..."</span></p>
                <p class="text-white/40">&#125;</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 03.3 COMPOUND -->
        <div class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] pt-12">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-4">03.3 · The Future: Compound</p>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] leading-tight mb-5">
                Keep your alpha. Control your costs.
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed mb-8">
                Instead of letting your "learning exhaust" go to waste, KYDE aggregates your agentic telemetry into a structured, private repository. This is where your organization's unique intelligence compounds.
              </p>
              <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#050505] overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="w-full font-mono text-xs">
                  <thead>
                    <tr class="border-b border-[#1F1F1F] text-[#6B6B6B] uppercase tracking-widest text-[10px]">
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3">Agent</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3">Provider</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3">Cost/Task</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3">Success</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#1F1F1F] text-[#A8A8A8]">
                    <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5">agent:support-02</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">OpenAI</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">$0.12</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">87%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5">agent:proc-7</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Anthropic</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">$0.41</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">64%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5">agent:hr-11</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Local/Llama</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">$0.02</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">91%</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              {[
                { label: "Vendor scorecards", desc: "Stop grading bots on marketing hype. KYDE tracks task completion rates, retry chains, and actual costs per transaction. Go to negotiation tables with hard data: “Your bot only solves 38% of our procurement tasks; we are renegotiating our contract.”" },
                { label: "Build your own learning loop", desc: "Collect your employees' corrections and successful trajectories to fine-tune small, hyper-efficient, local models. You get 10x cheaper task execution on models that you own entirely." },
                { label: "Decoupled orchestration", desc: "Keep your policies, memory, and evals on KYDE. If you switch from OpenAI to Anthropic tomorrow, your safety guards and learned behaviors remain perfectly intact." },
              ].map(({ label, desc }) => (
                <div class="flex items-start gap-4 border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#141414] p-4">
                  <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-[#3DDC84] mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
                  <div>
                    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F2F2F2] mb-0.5">{label}</p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-[#A8A8A8]">{desc}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 04 · WHY NOW ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#050505]">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24 md:border-x md:border-[#1F1F1F]">
        <div class="mb-12">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-[#1F1F1F] pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#A8A8A8]">04 · Why now?</span></div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] leading-tight mb-10 max-w-2xl">
          The marketplace is demanding accountability.
        </h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
          <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#0C0C0C] p-6 md:p-8">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-5">Defensive triggers</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              {[
                "NIS-2 (C-suite liability)",
                "DORA (financial resiliency)",
                "EU AI Act (audit trail duties)",
              ].map(item => (
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm text-[#A8A8A8]"><span class="font-mono shrink-0 mt-0.5">→</span>{item}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#0C0C0C] p-6 md:p-8">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-5">Offensive triggers</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              {[
                "Stopping token waste before it compounds",
                "Retaining proprietary IP, avoiding leakage",
                "Breaking vendor lock-in and monopoly pricing power",
              ].map(item => (
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm text-[#A8A8A8]"><span class="font-mono shrink-0 mt-0.5">→</span>{item}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Whether you are motivated by protecting your balance sheet from AI waste or protecting your board from regulatory liability, the answer is the same: <strong class="text-[#F2F2F2]">you must own your infrastructure.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 05 · DESIGN PARTNERSHIP ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-[#1F1F1F] bg-[#0C0C0C]">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 text-center py-16 md:py-24 md:border-x md:border-[#1F1F1F]">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#6B6B6B] mb-4">05 · Design Partnership Program</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#F2F2F2] mb-4">Secure your boundary today.</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-[#A8A8A8] mb-10 max-w-xl mx-auto">
          KYDE is built in partnership with leading, highly regulated enterprises in Europe and North America. We ensure your agentic workforce complies with NIS-2, DORA, GDPR, and the EU AI Act from day one.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center">
          <button
            onclick="openModal()"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white text-[#0A0A0A] px-8 py-4 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:bg-[#E5E5E5] transition-all"
          >
            Apply for Design Partnership →
          </button>
          <a
            href="/starter"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-[#2E2E2E] text-[#F2F2F2] px-8 py-4 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:border-white/40 transition-all"
          >
            Start Free →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
